# Implementation Acceptance Status

## Current Revision

As of 2026-11-01, the three accepted original 1448x1086 PNGs, tilted-hero
copy correction and phone image-before-prompt composition are verified.
The newly demonstrated reveal-cleanup race is fixed with guarded scalar
Motion updates. Native keyboard and exact-fraction hover helpers are
calibrated with positive and negative ordinary-control checks.

The frozen 807-input revision passes 138 files / 1633 non-DB tests, lint,
types, offline installed Prisma generation and the unmodified production
build. The full real-Next/synthetic-DB browser matrix passes **88/88 executable
checks**, including the new native reveal-interruption check. Two oversized
Unicode URL failures remain separate; they are not successful navigation.

The independent reviewers confirmed the new source/helper correction, but
provider quota interrupted the last reviewer's full final report. The
coordinator audited exact evidence, remaining source deltas and screenshots;
this does not impersonate an independent final sign-off. See
`final-continuation-review.md` for attribution and the remaining review gate.

Task status remains `in_progress`. No staging, commit, push, deployment or
archive is authorized. Earlier status records remain byte-for-byte in
`validation-evidence/browser-resume-records/` and
`validation-evidence/resume-01a190d3-records/`.

## Remaining Product Decision And Verification Limits

1. The existing query-string prefill cannot carry every 8000-unit Unicode
   prompt. ASCII 8000/8001 succeeds with the existing 8000-unit slice; 8000
   Chinese units encode to 72,015 request-target bytes and return HTTP 431;
   the tested emoji input encodes to 56,019 bytes and also returns 431.
   An explicit oversized-link/manual-copy fallback at the gallery entry is
   proposed but not approved. No threshold, storage, create/auth/draft or
   HTTP-limit workaround is implemented.
2. Local Node is 24.11.1, not pinned 24.22.1. No runtime is downloaded, and
   local checks do not establish pinned-runtime parity.
3. Actual Next/React/Chromium with a synthetic DB proves the tested UI and
   transfer contracts, not live-account/DB/Worker/provider/storage E2E,
   physical mobile/IME, actual CI or release readiness.
4. Independent final report/sign-off remains incomplete after a provider
   quota interruption. Its confirmed source findings and the coordinator's
   completed receipt/visual audit are recorded separately, not conflated.

